WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.534
-You look great.
I like the pink hair.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.000
I don't think I've ever seen
the pink hair on you.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.334
You look fantastic.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:07.834
-Thank-- I was going to say
I like your beard.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.801
-What?
This is like a compliment-off,

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.501
'cause I like your jacket.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.701
-Your suit's okay.

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.300
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.767
You got to have goals.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:23.734
-I've been going to the same
hair wizard for a while.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.100
That's what I call her,
my hair wizard.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.767
-Who is the hair wizard?
Do I know her?

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:29.267
-Her name is Marcy.
She's a big fan of yours.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:30.400
-Oh, hi, Marcy.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.968
-Wait, no, say, "Hola, Marcy."

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.367
-Hola, Marcy.
-Ooh.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.400
-She's a hair wizard you say?

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.901
-Yeah.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:42.234
Like, I feel like she -- one of
the first times I went to her,

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:45.067
she told me that she loves hair,

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:48.367
but she fears hair...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.300
...because hair is
like the ocean.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.801
It's full of secrets.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:57.968
So, I knew that I needed her.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.834
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.634
So, the hair is full of secrets.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:05.467
So, explain what happened
if you went to go see Marcy.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.701
-Well, what I love about her is
that she says,

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.767
"You don't tell me what to do.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.801
Your hair tells me what to do."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:16.234
So, I mean, I guess my hair
wanted to be pink.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.267
-Wow. She's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:21.467
It looks fantastic.
-You should go to Marcy.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.267
No, no, no.
-My hair has too many secrets.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.701
Julio, I wanted to ask you
a question because I know you

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:35.734
as a writer, as a stand-up --
a great stand-up, an actor.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:37.534
But you're getting
into something that's

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.667
a territory I know nothing
about.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.834
-Okay.
-This is hand acting.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.400
Do you know what
I'm talking about?

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.634
-Yeah, of course I know what
you're talking about.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.033
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.334
I meant to say that
to the audience.

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:48.901
Do you guys know
what I'm talking about?

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:52.734
Hand acting, can you explain to
everyone what this is?

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:56.701
-Yeah, I mean, I've seen a lot
of actors out there "acting,"

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:59.000
but then I look at their hands,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.467
and their hands aren't
quite performing.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:07.000
So, maybe I'll just show you.
Okay.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.501
So, I'm going to give you,
like, a few scenarios

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.934
and just some tricks
for actors out there

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.501
if they want to implement them.
-This is awesome.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:18.234
-Like for example, this would be
what you would do with a line

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:22.901
like, "Perhaps you can come to
my room later..."

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:26.334
"...and then
we can see what happens?"

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:33.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.801
-That just got
an eight-minute ovation

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:37.334
at the Venice Film Festival.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.334
-Yeah, yeah. Okay.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.634
I'm gonna give you another one.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.467
"Dolores, I need Roger
on the line."

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.968
That tells a story.
-Yes, Dolores.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:53.901
-Who is Dolores? Who is Roger?
-Of course, yeah.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.167
-Okay, I'm going to give you
another one.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:57.300
Do you have, like, a pen
and paper that I can borrow?

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.501
-Yeah.
-Oh, right there.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:02.133
Yeah. There, there, there.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.467
Okay. This is...

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:10.033
This is finally signing
the divorce papers.

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:17.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.467
-Oh, my good-- Wow!

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.133
Oh! Fine! Fine!

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.200
Ah, that's so -- Alright, fine!
You got me.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.767
-Do you have -- Do you have,
like, a cup or, like,

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:36.434
a wine glass or, like, a...

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.133
Yeah, with a stem. Yeah, that's
good. That's good.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.334
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:43.534
So, this is how you would
portray --

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:46.701
This is how only with your hands
you convey to the camera that,

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:50.167
"Yes, in fact,
there's poison in there."

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:56.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.701
-Yes, in fact, there is poison.
-There's poison.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:02.167
-There's poison in there.
-Do you have, like, a...

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:05.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.834
Do you have, like -- I want to
say, like, a vial of potion?

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:14.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:19.601
Okay. So, here.

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.534
You offer the potion.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:28.968
But you give a warning because
everything comes at a price.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:32.968
-Unbelievable.

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:36.300
That is why -- That's why
you're a professional.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.133
Unbelievable.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.000
-I'm a master.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.501
-"Los Espookys." Season two.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:46.067
I've been waiting for this
for a long time.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:50.100
I loved season one, and then you
were filming and then pandemic?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.000
-Yeah, so, we did season one.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.200
Then we were going to do
season two.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.400
And then this virus happened.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.267
-Mm. And then --
-Spread throughout the world.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.634
-So you shut down.
-So we had to shut down.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:08.934
So, we did almost four episodes,

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.868
and then we took a little break
for two years.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.801
-That's not --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:16.334
-We took -- They were like,
"Okay, we're breaking.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:19.300
Like, snack time for two years."

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.000
-Two years? Is that helpful? No.
That can't be helpful.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.434
-Some people are like, "Oh, that
must have been so awful."

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.501
And then it's like,

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:33.367
"Did we learn something through
stopping?"

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:35.634
No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.734
Was it good creatively?

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.667
Like, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:44.267
It was like, "actually I really,
really don't recommend --"

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:49.334
My advice would be,
if you are doing something

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:53.067
and it's going well, don't take
a break for two years.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:54.901
-Okay, that's good advice.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:57.000
How would you sum up the show
for us?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.634
-I would say,
"Watch it, please."

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:03.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:09.300
It's right -- You just open your
laptop and you da, da, da.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.000
And then you just watch it.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.133
-This is meant for
laptop viewing?

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:18.267
-I mean, let's face it,
how many -- you know.

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:19.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:22.667
I don't know.
Do you guys have televisions?

00:06:22.667 --> 00:06:24.534
-Yes, we all have televisions!

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:26.400
You're on it right now.
-I know.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.334
But, like, people are seeing it
on their phones.

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:32.067
-Oh, this is interesting.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:35.968
-There's this whole worldwide
web out there.

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:39.334
[ Laughter ]
-W-W-What?

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.701
Tell me about it.

00:06:40.701 --> 00:06:43.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:46.868
-No, watch it on TV.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:50.100
Here's Julio Torres in the new
season of "Los Espookys."

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.667
Take a look at this.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:53.100
-[ Speaking in Spanish ]

00:07:20.701 --> 00:07:22.868
-Julio Torres, everyone.

00:07:22.868 --> 00:07:26.868
Season two of "Los Espookys"
premieres September 16th

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:28.801
on HBO and HBO Max.

